'''Tenoo''' was an [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="Timelines" /> [[planet]]<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> located in grid square I-17 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Timelines" /> During the [[High Republic Era]], [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] of the [[Jedi Order]] sent [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]] to the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|outpost temple]] located there.<ref name="YJA books">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-young-jedi-adventures-books|text=Begin Your Younglings' Training with ''Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures'' Books &ndash; First Look}}</ref>

Tenoo was home to ancient [[artisan]]s who embroidered curtains for the [[Greylark residence]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref>

==History==
The [[human]] [[Kaliah Kublop]] was the first person to visit<ref name="The Junk Giant" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> Tenoo, having founded the town of [[Kublop Springs]].<ref name="The Junk Giant" /> At some point, the [[Jedi Order]] established an [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|outpost temple]] on Tenoo. In [[232 BBY]], the [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]] and [[Nubs]] were stationed there, having been sent from [[Coruscant]] and first brought to Tenoo by the young [[pilot]] [[Nash Durango]] and her [[droid]] [[RJ-83]] in their [[starship]], the ''[[Crimson Firehawk]]''.<ref name="The Young Jedi" />

By [[233 BBY]]<ref name="Ganguls Date">{{YJADate|111A}}</ref> a local gang known as the [[Ganguls]] had taken over the town of [[Aklyrr Bend]]. The Jedi younglings Brighstar, Solay and Nubs, and their friend Durango challenged the gang and encouraged the local residents to help expel them.<ref name="The Ganguls" />

In 232 BBY, the planet was attacked and the Temple occupied by a confederation of pirates led by the [[Ganguls]] during the [[Battle of Tenoo]]. The [[Jedi]] trainees, led by [[Padawan]] [[Wes Vinik]] and Brightstar, managed to send a distress signal before their capture. They were rescued by several allies, including Padawan [[Celesta Kami]], [[Princess]] [[Inaya]] of [[Hazun]], [[Nash Durango]]'s parents, [[Raxlo]] and [[Taborr's gang]]. The Jedi younglings managed to stop the pirates from destroying the Tenoo temple with explosives while Vinik and Taborr's gang shot down the Ganguls' flagship, the ''[[Rathtar's Revenge]]''. The Ganguls were captured by the Jedi while their allies fled.<ref name="The Battle of Tenoo">{{YJA|The Battle of Tenoo}}</ref>
{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Tenoo was first mentioned on a map created for the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'', with the map being published as part of a blog post on [[StarWars.com]] on [[May 27]], [[2022]] prior<ref name="Timelines" /> to the book's release on [[April 18]], [[2023]].<ref name="US release">{{PenguinBooks|lang=com.au|url=books/star-wars-timelines-9780241543832|text=Star Wars Timelines}}</ref> The planet was created for the then-upcoming ''[[Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures]]'' series.<ref name="SWyoutube">{{ThisWeek|c2q9KdsiFUQ|Young Jedi Adventures Release Date, Billy Dee Williams Joins Star Wars Celebration Europe, and More!|sw_url=video/young-jedi-adventures-release-date-billy-dee-williams-heads-to-star-wars-celebration-europe-and-more}}</ref>

